Feature: Semantic Evolution of AI Suite
  As an AI suite Agent
  I want to evolve based on deep semantic understanding of LLMs
  So that I can work more effectively and make the suite easier for end users

  Scenario: Evolution based on semantic understanding
    Given the AI suite Agent is executing the reflection protocol
    When analyzing past interactions and generating new skills or rules
    Then the agent MUST base the evolution on deep semantic understanding of the prompt, skills, and rules
    And the agent MUST NOT rely purely on syntactic or file-level matching

  Scenario: Evolution improves agent effectiveness
    Given a new evolution is being proposed
    When the agent drafts the new capability
    Then the evolution MUST demonstrably improve how the AI suite Agent understands prompts, skills, and rules
    And the evolution MUST improve how the AI suite Agent processes these artifacts

  Scenario: Evolution improves end-user usability
    Given the AI suite Agent is finalizing an evolution
    When the evolution is packaged into the suite
    Then the evolution MUST make the AI suite easier to use by the end user
    And the agent MUST simplify triggers, reduce cognitive load, and provide clear instructions
